{"name":"Tangled Twine","hex":"#b19466","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tangled","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Mixed up, interlaced.","Intricate."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of tangle"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tangled"},{"term":"twine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A twist; a convolution.","A strong thread composed of two or three smaller threads or strands twisted together, and used for various purposes, as for binding small parcels, making nets, and the like; a small cord or string."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To weave together.","To wind, as one thread around another, or as any flexible substance around another body."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tangled","blocks":[{"text":"Tangled is a 2010 American animated musical fantasy comedy film directed by Nathan Greno and Byron Howard, written by Dan Fogelman, and loosely based on the German fairy tale \"Rapunzel\". Produced by Walt Disney Animation Studios, it stars Mandy Moore, Zachary Levi, and Donna Murphy. The film tells the story of Rapunzel (Moore), a young princess with magical long blonde hair who tries to leave her secret tower. She accepts the aid of an intruder, the outlaw Flynn Rider (Levi), to take her out into the world which she has never seen."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a8/Tangled_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tangled","wikidata":"Q188439"},{"title":"Twine","blocks":[{"text":"Twine is a strong thread, light string or cord composed of string in which two or more thinner strands are twisted, and then twisted together (plied). The strands are plied in the opposite direction to that of their twist, which adds torsional strength to the cord and keeps it from unravelling. This process is sometimes called reverse wrap. The same technique used for making twine is also used to make thread, which is thinner, yarn, and rope, which is stronger and thicker, generally with three or more strands."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ae/Multiple_thread.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twine","wikidata":"Q762984"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Fragonard%2C_The_Swing.jpg/500px-Fragonard%2C_The_Swing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Fragonard%2C_The_Swing.jpg/1280px-Fragonard%2C_The_Swing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Fragonard%2C_The_Swing.jpg/500px-Fragonard%2C_The_Swing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Swing by Jean-Honoré Fragonard.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFragonard%2C_The_Swing.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1c/Rapunzel-Disney.jpg/250px-Rapunzel-Disney.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1c/Rapunzel-Disney.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1c/Rapunzel-Disney.jpg/250px-Rapunzel-Disney.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A concept rendering of Rapunzel by Lisa Keene, demonstrating the \"luscious golden hair\" Keane wanted.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARapunzel-Disney.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Making_Twine_%281915_by_Elstner_Hilton%29.jpg/500px-Making_Twine_%281915_by_Elstner_Hilton%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wi